<title>USA: Caterpillar's incentive pay rises for 1996.</title>
<headline>Caterpillar's incentive pay rises for 1996.</headline>
<dateline>PEORIA, Ill. 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Caterpillar Inc said Thursday its hourly, management and salaried employees next month will split a record $208 million in incentive pay and profit-sharing for 1996.</p>
<p>A company spokeswoman said the company distributed $134.7 million to its employees in 1995. The individual amounts will be determined by salary levels and by how much specific units added to Caterpillar's bottom line, she said.</p>
<p>The heavy equipment maker said the payouts reflect the contributions made by employees to help the company post record profits of $1.36 billion in 1996, up from $1.14 billion in 1995.</p>
<p>Caterpillar shares were down 5/8 Thursday at 80.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
